> [P]addy Cullen’s Pub in Dublin’s[ leaf]y Ballsbridge is an ideal location for the discerning customer to enjoy a drink[ or] fine food in good company and pleasant traditional surroundings.
Hugely popular around match-time,[ be] it Soccer or Rugby (thanks to its[ close] proximity to[ the] Aviva Stadium), there is[ always a good] atmosphere around the pub. They have a[ great] food menu, with[ everything] from[ Tap]as to a large selection of lunch and dinner[ options].
This is a[ great] spot[ to have] a pint of Dan Kelly’s Cider and[ definitely] worth a visit.
[Get] social with them on Facebook and Twitter.[]

